---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SchematicEditor from '../components/editor/SchematicEditor.tsx';
---

<Layout
  title="Circuit Simulator — Build & Simulate Online | CircuitSimLab"
  description="Free online circuit simulator. Drag components onto the canvas, wire them up, and run real DC, transient and AC analysis in your browser. No install, no sign-up."
  path="/simulator"
  bare
>
  <SchematicEditor client:only="react" />
  <noscript>
    <div class="container-page py-16">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">CircuitSimLab — Interactive Circuit Simulator</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2 max-w-2xl">
        The interactive circuit simulator requires JavaScript to run the schematic editor and the
        Modified Nodal Analysis (MNA) solver in your browser. Please enable JavaScript to use the
        full simulator experience.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">What you can do with the simulator</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 text-ink-2 space-y-2 list-disc ml-5">
        <li>Draw schematics by dragging components (resistors, capacitors, inductors, diodes, LEDs, transistors, voltage and current sources) onto a snapping grid.</li>
        <li>Wire terminals together with orthogonal auto-routing for clean connections.</li>
        <li>Run <strong>DC operating point</strong> analysis to find steady-state node voltages and branch currents.</li>
        <li>Run <strong>transient analysis</strong> to simulate circuits over time — watch capacitors charge, oscillators start, and signals propagate.</li>
        <li>Run <strong>AC frequency sweep</strong> analysis to find the frequency response of filters and amplifiers.</li>
        <li>Attach a virtual <strong>multimeter</strong> to read precise voltage and current values.</li>
        <li>Use a 2-channel <strong>oscilloscope</strong> with Volt/Div and Time/Div controls to inspect waveforms.</li>
        <li>Save projects locally, share circuits via URL, and export schematics as JSON.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Explore without JavaScript</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        While you need JavaScript for the interactive simulator, you can still explore these resources:
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="prose-link" href="/examples">Browse example circuits</a>
        <a class="prose-link" href="/learn">Learn electronics fundamentals</a>
        <a class="prose-link" href="/components">View the component library</a>
        <a class="prose-link" href="/documentation">Read the documentation</a>
        <a class="prose-link" href="/tools">Use electronics calculators</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </noscript>
</Layout>
